<description>&lt;p&gt;Egypt reopened its historic embassy in Tripoli after a 12‑year closure, restoring diplomatic presence and prompting regional officials to convene in the capital. ISIS militants killed a young Christian man who refused to deny Jesus, illustrating ongoing extremist violence. The WHO reported 111 children with malnutrition in Qatrun, warning of deteriorating health services. Migrant vessels departing from Libya have suffered deadly shipwrecks off Crete, with at least 20 migrants killed in recent incidents. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxQRkdEWnJyMlRPQkNYamR3SmpCSWxvSkNsNGM4anlaXzB4MTEzc0dwbldVVzZrMU5YZHhrcF9RaUFEWnl3djlqSmJ1ZUI3M3ZIOUtqTVhmTWdqNFp5enFnMXBjbFNkUkgxMDBZeHF0U2VjZWxQWGxmRnV6aWFiODZDSzNGUDZJaDlpNFN1QUpWRzFUSTE4amtZcFBKMk_SAZsBQVVfeXFMT1ZwQ3pVUm41SEprdXQ5QUt3ZDJaNEQ1aTdUbGlHZlhXbkRvRG11akdwSFhUNDR2OWozM0lfbGU2TXZSQVhPcVozUGp3WTYtUlBSV255MmpYNndSN3AzQXVvS0lnc0w3d1pSeXVkR2NfeFNzdzdqY0ZSQk5KUUJWejk0eDBZWEZJSWVoakdNNm1rLUhGNVFya3hLTG8?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQZkJ4MnRIOVFTNFpGTlVoWXhqRUFRbVBiNmlHN2czWE5tV19ZQW13ZUlRTDRSY2tFcG83WDVoY0lJVDZ3RkpuaHpSeVR0MndXLS1xaF8tOEROQlJYT0tKbjlZUHJiWDgyRXpRdml6UTNnV0ZGb3VjdG5ZRFVqSUU5ZzdBMXRZTHVCYUdkU1B1Z3hqQnVtZGpibEZnSHhKdjl2a0NoemFQRGhRYkc1YU5Lal9TNXRHYWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Libya Observer&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipAFBVV95cUxPUGZpcWFmSjZfUzNsalZGVnBaRjVoYi1fNnRheXo3YTh3ZmpEaHV3ZjdCb0hVcERWVnpCajBLTGRiQm4xMDNocWtJYVZRdW5HSFZZekpwSzVTeXJleTVjQVRRaG0yUkl1OU1EWFpPZWNoWHU2TWhLNFpZSzRyMFhvbkp1LTZtdWM1LW5sb3dBeThaOEgyNWtQel9jekJCZ2stVUpmeg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Ch